  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Order of work",
      "items": [
        "authorize runs before validation, so a forbidden caller learns nothing about the expected input.",
        "System actors (jobs, seed, CLI) pass every check; staff roles also need two-factor enabled.",
        "Every operation is registered by name and the RBAC matrix test calls each one with every role."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One transaction",
      "items": [
        "defineOperation only authorizes, validates and calls the handler.",
        "The handler writes the rows, the audit row and the job inside its own transaction.",
        "pg-boss writes the job row through that transaction, so there is no outbox table and the job exists only if the change commits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Worker and retries",
      "items": [
        "Each queue has its own retry count and backoff, for example payments.process-webhook 8 times and notify.email 5.",
        "Jobs that run out of retries land in system.dead-letter; a Super Admin can retry, discard or reprocess webhooks.",
        "cache.revalidate sends an HMAC-signed POST to every web replica; cron jobs run in Asia/Kolkata time."
      ]
    }
  ]
